 Griffiths/GKS-I: Cov(X_i,X_j) >= 0 holds EXACTLY in the FM (consec) regime, FAILS in AFM (dissociated).
 Caratheodory-Toeplitz: consec's miss-distribution q is CONVEX-DECREASING => positive-definite (Polya)
   => PSD Toeplitz = a valid circle measure = the ferromagnetic/ordered (rigid) phase; AFM breaks PSD.
 Verblunsky/Schur reflection coeffs |alpha_k|: closer to 1 = closer to the rigid boundary (finite support).
